      "label": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Catalyst discovery for the iron(III) porphyrin sulfonate-catalyzed glycosylation of glucuronals with glucuronic ester epoxides. aEpoxidation was carried out in a biphasic reaction medium with Oxone and acetone. The glycal epoxide was dried azeotropically with toluene, assayed by 1H NMR (dr >20:1), and then directly used. The glycosylation was carried out at 0 °C in CH2Cl2. Acetylation of 4a/4b was achieved using Ac2O/pyridine to afford 5a and 5b. bIsolated yield. The dr was determined by 1H NMR analysis. Iron(III) porphyrin catalysts 1a–1e were formed in situ from the corresponding iron porphy",
